{# ST-31 / ST-32 — Atemseite / breathing page (Plan B rebuild). DATA comes
   pre-shaped from patterns/st_31.py; this template only COMPOSES the geo_shapes
   overlay on the token-themed full-bleed .st-31 layout (styles/st_31.css).
   Fragment only — no <html>/<head>/<style>/@page/@font-face/:root (those live in
   the head).

   Structure: a single full-bleed atmospheric block (br-bleed) carrying the brand
   texture/gradient asset as a cover background (or a token gradient ground when
   no asset), with a low-opacity token-colored geometric accent overlay
   (geo_shapes — a quiet logo motif) and an OPTIONAL short centered statement. A
   deliberate pacing page. Checklist hits: #22 atmospheric/breathing page, #20
   low-opacity geometric shapes.

   WeasyPrint: the bleed block carries an explicit min-height (the full A4 sheet)
   so its background paints (an abspos inset:0 bg child paints 0 ink); the
   geo_shapes container + the optional statement are real children, so the block
   is never empty (an empty min-height-only flex box would not paint). #}
{% from 'geo_shapes.jinja' import geo_shapes %}
{% from 'phone_mockup.jinja' import phone_mockup %}

<div class="br-bleed{% if not has_ground %} br-bleed--gradient{% elif photo_ground %} br-bleed--photo{% endif %}"{{ ground_style }}>
  {# the atmospheric darken is ALWAYS painted (not gated on a phrase): it turns the
     ground — even a pale placeholder gradient — into a deliberate deep brand field
     (a designed pacing beat, like the back cover), never a washed-out blank page.
     Painted FIRST so the geo motif + any statement read ABOVE it. #}
  <div class="br-scrim"></div>
  {{ geo_shapes(variant) }}
  <div class="br-center">
    {% if has_social %}
    {# "live social presence": a renderer-drawn phone showing the founder's real
       IG post, centred on the deep brand ground (the geo motif frames it). #}
    <div class="br-phone">{{ phone_mockup(social_photo, avatar_uri=social_avatar, handle=social_handle, caption=social_caption, posts=(social_grid or None)) }}</div>
    {% elif phrase %}<p class="br-phrase">{{ phrase|e }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
